WEBVTT

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:15.750
Full energy is troubled because there's no place to go

00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:22.030
A slight shake destroys boredom

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:28.170
I Ride, On the White Line  OH, OH, OH

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:34.240
Sit Down  At the place I trust  OH, OH, OH

00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:37.540
We can go even if we're lost

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:43.650
Everyone receives freedom and passion

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:49.850
We were born to shine, and our journey continues

00:00:50.180 --> 00:00:56.060
Your soul is the key that supports our uncertain days

00:00:56.350 --> 00:01:02.000
The best growth creates an unstoppable WILD DRIVE

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:08.270
We still quietly knock on the door

00:01:19.970 --> 00:01:27.230
Honda showed up, but The Big Five was actually inside his body.

00:01:27.230 --> 00:01:32.200
The Big Five challenged us to a duel for our bodies.

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:38.080
We already beat them before, but we need to get Honda's body back.

00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:41.930
Jonouchi, we have to accept this duel.

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:49.020
Jonouchi Targeted
Team Play for Victory

00:02:05.890 --> 00:02:08.210
Starting now, you'll duel me.

00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:09.700
I draw!

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:13.580
Go easy on him, Jonouchi!

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:16.040
Don't attack him directly!

00:02:16.040 --> 00:02:17.800
Don't harm my body!

00:02:18.520 --> 00:02:21.950
Katsuya Jonouchi, I'll win this time.

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:24.460
I activate my Deck Master's ability!

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:27.390
Life Sentence!

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:29.780
What?  Already?

00:02:29.930 --> 00:02:33.960
By paying 1000 life points, I can make a verdict.

00:02:36.610 --> 00:02:38.290
Decision reversed!

00:02:38.290 --> 00:02:42.210
Your monsters will be banished.

00:02:45.150 --> 00:02:48.150
Our monsters were instantly destroyed!

00:02:48.150 --> 00:02:50.080
That's not all.

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:50.930
What?

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:57.760
Yes.  You take 500 points of damage for each banished monster.

00:03:10.130 --> 00:03:12.270
This is Kaiba Land.

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:29.520
This system...

00:03:32.360 --> 00:03:33.620
Checkmate.

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:48.510
What are you doing?

00:03:48.510 --> 00:03:50.020
You lost everything!

00:03:50.490 --> 00:03:51.920
It's fine, Honda.

00:03:51.920 --> 00:03:53.510
Let's believe in them.

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:56.950
You two have nothing.

00:03:57.350 --> 00:03:59.760
I summon Hysteric Angel!

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:04.120
Well now...

00:04:04.710 --> 00:04:08.170
That monkey said something interesting.

00:04:09.460 --> 00:04:12.750
Not to attack me directly.

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:16.670
In that case, I'll come at you!

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:21.270
Hysteric Angel attacks Katsuya Jonouchi directly!

00:04:29.310 --> 00:04:33.250
Damn.  Why couldn't Honda keep his mouth shut?

00:04:33.560 --> 00:04:36.920
My attack isn't over.

00:04:36.920 --> 00:04:42.120
Next, Catapult Turtle fires Hysteric Angel!

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:50.400
Jonouchi!

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:51.270
Brother!

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:55.300
This is bad.  He's only going after Jonouchi.

00:04:56.660 --> 00:04:57.710
Jonouchi...

00:04:58.110 --> 00:05:00.090
Are you okay, Jonouchi?

00:05:00.090 --> 00:05:01.650
Damn.

00:05:02.750 --> 00:05:07.300
Yugi is a high level duelist.  I don't need to go after him first.

00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:10.080
Defeat the weak one first.

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:12.390
That's the best way to fight.

00:05:12.620 --> 00:05:15.080
Keep making excuses.

00:05:15.280 --> 00:05:18.950
The truth is: You're mad that you lost to me!

00:05:19.860 --> 00:05:21.950
Say whatever you want.

00:05:22.370 --> 00:05:24.300
I set a card.

00:05:24.580 --> 00:05:28.460
Then I activate the spell card, Altar of Mist!

00:05:28.980 --> 00:05:30.430
Altar of Mist.

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:33.980
It lets him get a Ritual Spell in three turns.

00:05:34.220 --> 00:05:41.050
And spells, traps and effects can't destroy that card.

00:05:41.800 --> 00:05:43.490
I end my turn.

00:05:43.490 --> 00:05:45.920
My turn!  I draw!

00:05:47.690 --> 00:05:49.480
Nice!  Here I go!

00:05:49.480 --> 00:05:51.280
I summon Rocket Warrior!

00:05:53.730 --> 00:05:59.240
In my last duel, I used my Deck Master's ability too early, so I had trouble later.

00:05:59.240 --> 00:06:01.370
So I saved it this time.

00:06:01.370 --> 00:06:04.380
But with only 300 life points left, I can't wait.

00:06:04.620 --> 00:06:07.310
I activate my Deck Master's ability!

00:06:07.770 --> 00:06:12.450
Flame Swordsman transfers 1000 attack points to Rocket Warrior!

00:06:13.880 --> 00:06:17.890
Go!  Rocket Warrior attacks Catapult Turtle!

00:06:20.770 --> 00:06:24.570
I activate the Quick-Play Spell, Revenge Sacrifice!

00:06:24.570 --> 00:06:25.810
What?

00:06:25.810 --> 00:06:30.270
When my monster is destroyed in battle...

00:06:30.500 --> 00:06:34.440
...I tribute your monster that destroyed mine.

00:06:34.760 --> 00:06:37.700
And I Special Summon from my hand.

00:06:38.860 --> 00:06:41.110
I turn everything to my advantage.

00:06:41.380 --> 00:06:43.530
I summon Machine King!

00:06:45.200 --> 00:06:53.290
It gains 100 attack points for every Machine-Type monster on the field, including itself.

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:55.960
I end my turn.

00:06:55.960 --> 00:06:57.800
I'm counting on you, Yugi!

00:06:58.480 --> 00:06:59.230
Yeah.

00:06:59.700 --> 00:07:04.320
But the only monster card I have in my hand is Des Volstgalph.

00:07:04.740 --> 00:07:07.760
I can't summon it without tributing.

00:07:08.170 --> 00:07:10.400
It all depends on my next draw.

00:07:10.660 --> 00:07:12.880
My turn!  I draw!

00:07:14.180 --> 00:07:15.950
The Rock Spirit.

00:07:16.460 --> 00:07:22.390
I can Special Summon this monster by banishing an Earth Attribute Monster from my graveayrd.

00:07:23.240 --> 00:07:27.680
I used Card Destruction to send Buster Blader to the graveyard.

00:07:28.640 --> 00:07:31.330
I banish Buster Blader from my graveyard!

00:07:32.640 --> 00:07:35.370
I Special Summon The Rock Spirit!

00:07:37.970 --> 00:07:43.430
I tribute The Rock Spirit to summon Des Volstgalph!

00:07:49.040 --> 00:07:54.220
Yugi, it has 100 fewer attack points than Machine King's 2300 points.

00:07:54.630 --> 00:07:56.150
What will you do?

00:07:56.150 --> 00:07:58.820
I set one card.

00:07:59.660 --> 00:08:00.760
I end my turn.

00:08:01.920 --> 00:08:05.390
Oh no!  What's gotten into you, Yugi?

00:08:05.390 --> 00:08:07.800
That move is too obvious!

00:08:08.170 --> 00:08:11.720
It's like you're telling him that you played a trap!

00:08:13.510 --> 00:08:16.040
What's Jonouchi doing?

00:08:16.660 --> 00:08:19.280
Brother, get serious!

00:08:19.280 --> 00:08:21.970
He is serious.

00:08:21.970 --> 00:08:22.810
What?

00:08:23.020 --> 00:08:29.360
Even beginners like us can tell that Yugi's strategy is bad.

00:08:29.820 --> 00:08:32.360
That's why Jonouchi is worried.

00:08:32.360 --> 00:08:36.060
Why did Yugi make that move?

00:08:39.160 --> 00:08:42.780
Good job on summoning Machine King, Ooka.

00:08:42.780 --> 00:08:44.740
Don't get the wrong idea!

00:08:44.740 --> 00:08:46.450
My intention wasn't to-

00:08:46.450 --> 00:08:47.450
Silence!

00:08:47.850 --> 00:08:52.170
Since I'm the factory manager, Machine King is perfect for me!

00:08:52.170 --> 00:08:58.970
I, Soichiro Ota, and my Deck Master, Robotic Knight, will fight you!

00:08:58.970 --> 00:08:59.850
It's him!

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:02.480
The man who turned Honda into a monkey.

00:09:03.450 --> 00:09:05.290
My turn.  I draw!

00:09:05.500 --> 00:09:10.910
He summoned a monster with fewer attack points than Machine King and set a card.

00:09:11.340 --> 00:09:12.850
How dangerous.

00:09:14.200 --> 00:09:17.540
If you're setting a trap, make it less obvious.

00:09:19.300 --> 00:09:21.150
Seems I was right.

00:09:21.150 --> 00:09:23.810
See?  He easily figured it out!

00:09:23.810 --> 00:09:28.240
But Yugi must have some plan.

00:09:28.240 --> 00:09:32.550
Such an obvious strategy!  Don't mock me, kid!

00:09:32.760 --> 00:09:35.280
The spell card, Heavy Storm!

00:09:36.660 --> 00:09:40.800
All spell and trap cards on the field are destroyed!

00:09:45.530 --> 00:09:48.110
Mirror Force, eh?

00:09:48.800 --> 00:09:50.260
That's right.

00:09:50.260 --> 00:09:54.870
If you attacked with a monster, I was going to strike you back.

00:09:55.080 --> 00:09:59.250
Huh?  Yugi, you didn't have another plan?

00:09:59.250 --> 00:10:00.810
Sorry, Jonouchi.

00:10:00.810 --> 00:10:02.280
Sorry?

00:10:02.740 --> 00:10:06.750
Are you underestimating The Big Five?

00:10:06.750 --> 00:10:10.100
Exactly.  You underestimate us.

00:10:10.100 --> 00:10:11.570
Get ready, kid!

00:10:11.780 --> 00:10:13.360
Machine King!

00:10:13.600 --> 00:10:15.290
Wait!  This is a trap!

00:10:15.500 --> 00:10:18.140
Attack Des Volstgalph!

00:10:20.540 --> 00:10:21.680
You fell for it!

00:10:21.680 --> 00:10:22.480
What?

00:10:22.480 --> 00:10:25.220
I had two traps.

00:10:25.220 --> 00:10:28.700
Whatever!  There are no traps on the field!

00:10:29.100 --> 00:10:30.370
I'll show you.

00:10:31.160 --> 00:10:40.820
During battle, Des Volstgalph gains 200 attack points for every spell card used this turn.

00:10:40.820 --> 00:10:45.280
Say what?  Since I used Heavy Storm...

00:10:46.320 --> 00:10:49.640
Strike back, Des Volstgalph!

00:10:55.800 --> 00:10:57.600
What?

00:10:58.640 --> 00:11:01.300
I tricked an adult.

00:11:01.660 --> 00:11:06.600
Due to Des Volstgalph's effect, you lose 500 life points.

00:11:06.600 --> 00:11:08.300
How insolent!

00:11:08.300 --> 00:11:10.640
But it's only 600 points.

00:11:10.640 --> 00:11:13.280
That strategy isn't worth bragging about!

00:11:13.630 --> 00:11:15.030
You're wrong.

00:11:15.030 --> 00:11:18.940
His strategy had a different goal.

00:11:18.940 --> 00:11:19.720
What?

00:11:20.060 --> 00:11:22.220
I see!  I get it!

00:11:22.220 --> 00:11:23.160
What?

00:11:23.520 --> 00:11:28.330
What if he attacked Jonouchi instead of Yugi this turn?

00:11:28.330 --> 00:11:31.560
Since Jonouchi doesn't have any monsters...

00:11:32.400 --> 00:11:34.770
He would've been attacked directly.

00:11:34.980 --> 00:11:40.550
Yes.  Since Jonouchi only has 300 life points, he would've lost.

00:11:41.600 --> 00:11:44.570
Yugi wanted to be attacked.

00:11:44.570 --> 00:11:47.750
So he provoked him by using an obvious strategy.

00:11:47.960 --> 00:11:52.150
I see.  Yugi, you were thinking about me.

00:11:52.360 --> 00:11:55.960
Jonouchi, the way you were panicking?  Nice acting!

00:11:57.700 --> 00:12:00.560
Jonouchi was pretending to panic?

00:12:00.560 --> 00:12:03.770
Really?  I couldn't tell!

00:12:04.730 --> 00:12:06.330
They fooled them!

00:12:06.780 --> 00:12:08.770
Brother, you're incredible!

00:12:09.000 --> 00:12:11.510
Huh?  Uhh... Yeah!

00:12:11.510 --> 00:12:12.680
Exactly!

00:12:15.240 --> 00:12:18.610
I was almost turned into a monkey robot.

00:12:19.660 --> 00:12:21.520
I end my turn.

00:12:22.020 --> 00:12:25.520
You missed your chance to defeat that kid.

00:12:25.520 --> 00:12:27.860
Your time is up.

00:12:28.780 --> 00:12:31.490
I'm up next turn!

00:12:48.300 --> 00:12:49.380
My turn!

00:12:49.760 --> 00:12:52.380
He has no monsters to defend with.

00:12:52.380 --> 00:12:54.550
I can attack him directly.

00:12:54.550 --> 00:12:56.850
Let me get a monster card!

00:12:57.100 --> 00:12:58.020
I draw!

00:12:58.330 --> 00:12:59.820
Yeah!  I got one!

00:12:59.820 --> 00:13:00.690
I'll use it to-

00:13:02.960 --> 00:13:07.290
Panther Warrior can't attack unless I tribute another monster.

00:13:07.290 --> 00:13:11.170
Damn!  This was the perfect chance to strike back!

00:13:11.680 --> 00:13:12.970
Oh well.

00:13:14.330 --> 00:13:17.300
I summon Panther Warrior in defense position!

00:13:18.240 --> 00:13:21.480
But I won't let him draw next turn.

00:13:22.520 --> 00:13:25.410
I set a card and end my turn.

00:13:25.680 --> 00:13:27.360
I'm counting on you, Yugi.

00:13:27.360 --> 00:13:28.420
Yeah.

00:13:28.420 --> 00:13:29.820
My turn!

00:13:29.820 --> 00:13:30.520
I draw!

00:13:30.900 --> 00:13:32.510
Sorry, Honda.

00:13:32.510 --> 00:13:34.960
But this is my chance to beat him!

00:13:34.960 --> 00:13:36.740
I know...

00:13:36.740 --> 00:13:39.250
Go all out, Yugi!

00:13:39.250 --> 00:13:40.890
It'll be fine, Honda.

00:13:40.890 --> 00:13:44.230
Des Volstgalph, attack him directly!

00:13:50.760 --> 00:13:55.120
I summon Big Shield Gardna in defense position!

00:13:56.380 --> 00:13:57.810
I end my turn.

00:13:59.060 --> 00:14:01.020
Two turns left...

00:14:06.900 --> 00:14:08.860
It's empty.

00:14:45.540 --> 00:14:51.770
Noa, are you showing me this to prove that you're Gozaburo's son?

00:15:04.540 --> 00:15:05.910
What?

00:15:07.380 --> 00:15:09.620
Noa is dead?

00:15:09.620 --> 00:15:14.000
Then who's the Noa that we met?

00:15:20.450 --> 00:15:24.370
Why is he showing me this?

00:15:29.250 --> 00:15:32.870
Maybe Noa didn't create this program?

00:15:38.000 --> 00:15:41.580
I, Kogoro Daimon, will now duel.

00:15:41.970 --> 00:15:44.510
I'm not like the others.

00:15:44.510 --> 00:15:45.940
Get ready.

00:15:46.310 --> 00:15:48.780
Stop bragging and make your move!

00:15:49.440 --> 00:15:50.190
I draw-

00:15:50.390 --> 00:15:53.160
Stop!  I won't let you draw!

00:15:53.160 --> 00:15:55.530
The trap card, Drop Off!

00:15:55.780 --> 00:15:59.280
The card you drew goes straight to the graveyard!

00:15:59.280 --> 00:16:00.450
You sure?

00:16:01.840 --> 00:16:02.800
What?

00:16:04.270 --> 00:16:07.350
I get it!  Your Deck Master is...

00:16:08.700 --> 00:16:12.810
Yes.  My Deck Master is Jinzo.

00:16:13.260 --> 00:16:15.750
Damn.  He outsmarted me.

00:16:16.020 --> 00:16:19.500
You should've let me duel from the start.

00:16:20.770 --> 00:16:22.620
I'm going to keep drawing.

00:16:22.990 --> 00:16:27.050
Due to Pot of Greed, I draw two more cards.

00:16:30.300 --> 00:16:35.220
Since you used a spell card, Des Volstgalph's effect activates!

00:16:35.220 --> 00:16:37.800
It gains 200 attack points!

00:16:37.800 --> 00:16:39.300
So what?

00:16:39.300 --> 00:16:42.620
I summon Injection Fairy Lily.

00:16:47.860 --> 00:16:51.620
You put a monster with 400 attack points in attack position?

00:16:51.620 --> 00:16:53.420
No, Jonouchi!  That's-

00:16:53.420 --> 00:16:56.920
Do you think I'd do that without having a plan?

00:16:56.920 --> 00:16:57.960
You fool.

00:16:57.960 --> 00:16:58.860
What?

00:16:59.220 --> 00:17:07.530
By paying 2000 life points, Injection Fairy Lily gains 3000 attack points during damage calculation.

00:17:08.000 --> 00:17:09.470
3000 points?

00:17:09.470 --> 00:17:12.110
Go!  Injection Fairy Lily!

00:17:12.110 --> 00:17:14.400
It's time for a checkup!

00:17:17.620 --> 00:17:18.710
Injection!

00:17:22.670 --> 00:17:26.600
He's willing to lose many life points to attack.

00:17:27.570 --> 00:17:28.950
Don't worry.

00:17:28.950 --> 00:17:30.980
I have a great follow-up.

00:17:30.980 --> 00:17:33.540
The Quick-Play Spell, Sebek's Blessing.

00:17:35.000 --> 00:17:36.800
Sebek's Blessing?

00:17:36.800 --> 00:17:42.170
He regains life points equal to damage he dealt.

00:17:42.680 --> 00:17:48.840
Exactly.  I regain 1000 life points.

00:17:48.840 --> 00:17:51.850
I set one card.

00:17:52.010 --> 00:17:53.640
I end my turn.

00:17:54.500 --> 00:17:56.870
It's your turn, Jonouchi!

00:17:56.870 --> 00:17:59.450
I know!  You don't need to tell me!

00:17:59.660 --> 00:18:05.390
But how can I destroy a monster with 3400 attack points?

00:18:05.620 --> 00:18:10.600
Just because it's 2-on-1, we shouldn't have let him have 8000 life points.

00:18:11.900 --> 00:18:13.830
I'll make it even harder for you.

00:18:14.280 --> 00:18:15.770
My set card is...

00:18:16.620 --> 00:18:20.120
Gravity Bind!

00:18:20.870 --> 00:18:25.650
Level 4-and-above monsters can't attack.

00:18:25.880 --> 00:18:30.650
What?  Jinzo's effect should destroy that trap!

00:18:30.650 --> 00:18:36.590
My Deck Master's ability doesn't destroy my own traps.

00:18:36.800 --> 00:18:38.000
Damn!

00:18:38.000 --> 00:18:38.760
I draw!

00:18:39.500 --> 00:18:40.690
All right!

00:18:40.960 --> 00:18:43.700
I'll also play Jinzo!

00:18:43.700 --> 00:18:46.130
It can destroy his trap.

00:18:46.570 --> 00:18:51.340
I tribute Panther Warrior to summon Jinzo!

00:18:54.910 --> 00:18:59.100
An eye for an eye, a Jinzo for a Jinzo.

00:18:59.100 --> 00:19:00.910
Here's payback!

00:19:00.910 --> 00:19:01.980
Trap Search!

00:19:08.620 --> 00:19:09.820
How's that!

00:19:10.020 --> 00:19:11.920
You think you won?

00:19:11.920 --> 00:19:13.040
What?

00:19:13.040 --> 00:19:19.100
You destroyed my trap, but Injection Fairy Lily still has 3400 attack points.

00:19:19.100 --> 00:19:23.880
How can you win when Jinzo has 2400 attack points?

00:19:24.980 --> 00:19:27.120
That was careless, Jonouchi!

00:19:27.120 --> 00:19:32.200
Did you forget that Lily gains attack points when she attacks?

00:19:32.200 --> 00:19:33.140
Yugi...

00:19:33.360 --> 00:19:35.620
ONLY her attack points.

00:19:37.580 --> 00:19:40.070
She only gains attack points...

00:19:40.500 --> 00:19:41.650
Only...

00:19:42.200 --> 00:19:43.420
I get it!

00:19:44.120 --> 00:19:47.360
Only Lily's attack points rise.

00:19:47.360 --> 00:19:49.350
Her defense points stay the same.

00:19:50.030 --> 00:19:53.220
Okay!  The spell card, Block Attack!

00:19:53.800 --> 00:19:57.500
I switch Injection Fairy Lily to defense position!

00:19:58.330 --> 00:19:59.070
What?

00:20:01.510 --> 00:20:02.760
Here I go!

00:20:02.760 --> 00:20:06.760
Jinzo attacks Injection Fairy Lily!

00:20:06.760 --> 00:20:08.760
Cyber Energy Shock!

00:20:12.460 --> 00:20:14.930
He has no monsters left.

00:20:14.930 --> 00:20:16.960
I leave the rest to you, Yugi.

00:20:16.960 --> 00:20:18.130
I end my turn!

00:20:18.540 --> 00:20:19.340
Yeah.

00:20:19.340 --> 00:20:21.420
My turn!  I draw!

00:20:23.460 --> 00:20:26.000
I tribute Big Shield Gardna.

00:20:26.730 --> 00:20:29.130
I summon Dark Magician Girl!

00:20:31.160 --> 00:20:33.580
Go!  Dark Magician Girl!

00:20:33.580 --> 00:20:35.140
Attack him directly!

00:20:42.690 --> 00:20:45.050
Nice, Yugi!  We're almost done!

00:20:47.240 --> 00:20:48.490
I end my turn.

00:20:51.500 --> 00:20:53.560
It's too early to celebrate.

00:20:54.120 --> 00:20:56.760
I was waiting for this moment.

00:20:57.180 --> 00:20:58.520
Waiting?

00:20:59.060 --> 00:21:00.100
Altar of Mist!

00:21:00.100 --> 00:21:04.320
Yes.  It's the third turn since Altar of Mist's activation.

00:21:06.360 --> 00:21:08.660
My turn.  I draw.

00:21:12.820 --> 00:21:14.010
What is it?

00:21:17.860 --> 00:21:19.440
What's so funny?

00:21:20.960 --> 00:21:23.120
This duel is over!

00:21:23.440 --> 00:21:24.290
What?

00:21:24.680 --> 00:21:29.730
When I summon this monster, your odds of victory is 0!

00:21:43.370 --> 00:21:48.040
The Big Five activates the spell card, Altar of Mist.

00:21:48.040 --> 00:21:52.090
That card summons Five-Headed Dragon.

00:21:52.090 --> 00:21:57.000
By tributing the five Deck Masters, Five-Headed Dragon shows its enormous figure.

00:21:57.000 --> 00:22:01.320
You can't summon Dragon Master Knight without Blue-Eyes.

00:22:01.320 --> 00:22:05.400
Yugi and Jonouchi, do you have a monster that can fight it?

00:22:05.400 --> 00:22:08.720
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Defeat Five-Headed Dragon

00:22:08.720 --> 00:22:10.240
Duel, standby!

00:22:13.420 --> 00:22:21.320
The sun never sets
It rises forever

00:22:21.320 --> 00:22:30.270
Don't let a dream end as a dream

00:22:30.600 --> 00:22:35.240
The straight rail and harsh route

00:22:35.240 --> 00:22:39.210
Whether to go or not 
all of yourself

00:22:39.640 --> 00:22:47.180
I'm tired of counting on my fingers inside this cage

00:22:47.180 --> 00:22:50.750
Respect! Boys  Show me how you act tough

00:22:50.750 --> 00:22:55.520
Draw a map, even if it's sloppy

00:22:55.520 --> 00:23:05.630
And walk it without stopping

00:23:05.630 --> 00:23:13.240
The sun never sets
If I can be like you

00:23:13.470 --> 00:23:22.210
Create freedom by exceeding common ideas

00:23:22.210 --> 00:23:30.190
I want to trust myself
Sometimes I'll lose my way but

00:23:30.190 --> 00:23:40.030
I hide it in my heart...
Secret Paradise
